  <!-- 9. MOBILE NAVIGATION DRAWER -->
  <Section bg="page" padding="sm" id="mobile-nav">
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="09. Responsive Navigation"
        title="Mobile Navigation Drawer & Touch Architecture"
        lead="Progressively enhanced mobile drawer with min 44px touch targets, Escape dismissal, and outside click management."
      />

      <div class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-border-subtle rounded-md shadow-subtle max-w-xl">
        <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-brand-navy mb-2">Mobile Drawer Features</h4>
        <ul class="text-xs text-brand-charcoal/80 space-y-2 mb-6 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>Accessible trigger button:</strong> Enforces <code class="font-mono">aria-expanded</code> and <code class="font-mono">aria-controls</code> attributes.</li>
          <li><strong>Focus security:</strong> Panel is strictly <code class="font-mono">hidden</code> when closed, preventing keyboard focus on collapsed links.</li>
          <li><strong>Escape dismissal:</strong> Pressing Escape immediately closes the drawer and restores focus to the trigger.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean resize:</strong> Automatically collapses when the viewport expands to desktop (<code class="font-mono">&ge; 1024px</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>No-JS fallback:</strong> Progressively enhanced; renders accessible fallback in <code class="font-mono">&lt;noscript&gt;</code> environments.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted">
          Resize the browser window below <code class="font-mono">1024px</code> or inspect the mobile preview above to test the drawer interactions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

